WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.041 --> 00:00:06.548
♪♪♪

00:00:06.548 --> 00:00:07.632
-[Kalin Bennett:] Growin' up, a lot of people

00:00:07.632 --> 00:00:08.717
didn't even know I had autism.

00:00:09.634 --> 00:00:10.844
I just started tellin' people,

00:00:10.844 --> 00:00:11.886
like, last year.

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:14.514
Cuz I was like, "You know what?

00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:15.807
I don't know why people not

00:00:15.807 --> 00:00:17.058
knowin' about me."

00:00:17.058 --> 00:00:18.601
Like, everything just exploded.

00:00:19.936 --> 00:00:21.771
Fast forward to my senior year,

00:00:21.771 --> 00:00:23.356
I just signed with a D1 college.

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:28.570
I'm humbled, honored. But at the same time,

00:00:28.570 --> 00:00:30.071
I mean, I'm still Kalin.

00:00:30.071 --> 00:00:38.580
♪♪♪

00:00:39.914 --> 00:00:44.461
♪♪♪

00:00:44.461 --> 00:00:46.337
-[Julian Sullinger:] I want you to look at this segment, too.

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:49.424
You roll out, and I'mma tell you,

00:00:49.424 --> 00:00:51.426
you already know what I'mma tell you about this one.

00:00:51.843 --> 00:00:52.969
- I shoulda dunked that.

00:00:52.969 --> 00:00:53.970
- Yeah?

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:56.097
- I shoulda, I shoulda dunked that.

00:00:56.097 --> 00:00:58.016
- Yeah. I tell you this all the time.

00:00:58.224 --> 00:01:00.018
When you go in, when you do your five-on-five

00:01:00.018 --> 00:01:02.270
or five-on-0, you tear the rim down right here.

00:01:04.105 --> 00:01:05.273
- Yes, sir.

00:01:06.566 --> 00:01:09.194
All these college didn't even know

00:01:09.194 --> 00:01:12.781
I had autism until I said it.

00:01:12.781 --> 00:01:14.824
Kent State, I wanted to come here cuz of

00:01:14.824 --> 00:01:18.745
the culture and the basketball and the people.

00:01:18.745 --> 00:01:20.538
I had to make that known because

00:01:20.538 --> 00:01:22.123
I don't want people to, like, think I'm just,

00:01:22.123 --> 00:01:25.335
like, given something because of something I have.

00:01:25.627 --> 00:01:27.754
- I recruited him becuase I thought

00:01:27.754 --> 00:01:29.172
there was a chance for him to be

00:01:29.172 --> 00:01:30.882
a really good baskeball player.

00:01:30.882 --> 00:01:32.342
The fact the he has autism is the

00:01:32.342 --> 00:01:35.804
story for him, but at the same time,

00:01:35.804 --> 00:01:38.598
he's a basketball player who's tryin' to figure out

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:40.558
how to be the best college player he can be.

00:01:40.892 --> 00:01:42.602
- The offers and everything I have,

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:44.562
I completely earned.

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:47.565
I mean a lotta people did not

00:01:47.565 --> 00:01:48.733
expect me to be here.

00:01:48.733 --> 00:01:50.527
♪♪♪

00:01:50.527 --> 00:01:50.693
♪♪♪

00:01:50.777 --> 00:01:53.655
I was born and raised in Little Rock, Arkansas.

00:01:53.655 --> 00:01:54.781
I went to high school at

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:56.157
Little Rock Christian Academy.

00:01:57.992 --> 00:02:00.703
When people hear "autism", they don't understand.

00:02:00.703 --> 00:02:03.206
Like sometimes, they feel like that's an insult.

00:02:03.206 --> 00:02:05.875
That's not what it means at all.

00:02:05.875 --> 00:02:07.418
That means maybe they're somebody

00:02:07.418 --> 00:02:10.255
who does things differently, somebody who

00:02:10.255 --> 00:02:12.298
has a higher IQ, maybe they're somebody

00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:14.968
who has, like, sensory overload.

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:17.679
You never know what that person is goin' through

00:02:17.679 --> 00:02:20.598
in the inside. Cuz it - autism, to me, also is an

00:02:20.598 --> 00:02:23.601
inside struggle. Not a lotta people understand it

00:02:23.601 --> 00:02:25.228
becuase they only see it from the outside.

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:29.232
- I didn't find out officially that

00:02:29.232 --> 00:02:34.779
Kalin had autism until he was about two.

00:02:35.905 --> 00:02:40.076
He wasn't focusing on me. No sound at all,

00:02:40.076 --> 00:02:42.829
not even a cry. And didn't want to be touched

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:44.414
at that young age.

00:02:45.248 --> 00:02:47.667
- [Kalin:] I didn't walk until I was four,

00:02:47.667 --> 00:02:49.335
and I didn't talk until I was seven.

00:02:50.086 --> 00:02:53.256
- Doctors, they told me that it was a bunch of "nevers".

00:02:53.256 --> 00:02:57.343
Never walk. Never talk. Wouldn't go to regular school

00:02:57.343 --> 00:02:59.637
with regular children.

00:02:59.637 --> 00:03:01.806
- If you say "can't" in front of her, she's gonna

00:03:01.806 --> 00:03:04.058
make sure she's either gonna prove you wrong, or

00:03:04.058 --> 00:03:06.311
she's gonna shut you down once you say that word.

00:03:06.311 --> 00:03:08.855
- I'm sittin' up there lookin' like, "Yes, he will."

00:03:08.855 --> 00:03:12.275
"Mrs. Bennett, you need to just come to grips."

00:03:12.275 --> 00:03:15.028
So I gripped my purse, and I left out.

00:03:15.028 --> 00:03:18.239
- My mom had a file about, like, my test results,

00:03:18.239 --> 00:03:21.701
you know, evaluations. And so, like, I was looking at

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:23.703
the first test score, which is super low,

00:03:23.703 --> 00:03:25.830
then a recent score, which is super high,

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:28.666
and I just broke down cryin'. Cuz I was like,

00:03:28.666 --> 00:03:30.501
"Look where I came from and look where I am now."

00:03:30.501 --> 00:03:34.005
♪♪♪

00:03:36.007 --> 00:03:38.009
- I made sure to celebrate an early birthday

00:03:38.009 --> 00:03:40.136
with the people that's in Arkansas, cuz, like, I'm

00:03:40.136 --> 00:03:42.430
not gonna have most of the people here.

00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:45.058
All I ever wanted in my life was

00:03:45.058 --> 00:03:47.477
all my family in one room.

00:03:48.436 --> 00:03:52.148
[Cheering and applause]

00:03:52.148 --> 00:03:54.859
- This is just a, just a opportunity to just

00:03:54.859 --> 00:03:57.570
thank all of you. Like, I know this is celebrating me,

00:03:57.570 --> 00:04:01.407
but this is a chance for me to thank all of you.

00:04:01.407 --> 00:04:04.827
Because there's no way that I would be here without

00:04:04.827 --> 00:04:06.829
every single one of you. There's no way.

00:04:09.999 --> 00:04:12.669
- [Kalin:] We're getting ready to move to Ohio today.

00:04:12.669 --> 00:04:14.754
We packed up the car, my mom's coming, and

00:04:14.754 --> 00:04:15.922
we about to move out.

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:19.008
- I'm asking that you would strengthen all four

00:04:19.008 --> 00:04:21.928
of my grandbabies, God. Give them the strength to

00:04:21.928 --> 00:04:24.889
be able to make this trip, God. In the name of Jesus

00:04:24.889 --> 00:04:26.933
we pray, amen.

00:04:28.768 --> 00:04:31.187
- Group hug.

00:04:34.649 --> 00:04:36.693
- [Sonja:] Love y'all!

00:04:36.693 --> 00:04:39.445
♪♪♪ 

00:04:39.445 --> 00:04:42.824
- It's a thousand miles away from most of my family.

00:04:42.824 --> 00:04:45.201
I have no idea who these people are. The only

00:04:45.201 --> 00:04:47.578
people I know is my teammates and my coach.

00:04:47.578 --> 00:04:51.082
Like, there's no one here. I'm excited because, like,

00:04:51.082 --> 00:04:54.002
there might not be, like, as many as distractions

00:04:54.002 --> 00:04:56.963
to me as there would be in Arkansas. I think it's

00:04:56.963 --> 00:05:00.341
good for me to be in, like, a whole new surrounding,

00:05:00.341 --> 00:05:02.885
whole new place, and, like, a whole new culture.

00:05:02.885 --> 00:05:04.262
I'm excited.

00:05:05.388 --> 00:05:07.849
- The biggest thing that, that drew me to him

00:05:07.849 --> 00:05:11.269
was his enthusiasm. Always positive. Always

00:05:11.269 --> 00:05:13.980
bringin' tremendous energy, and when you see that

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:16.524
in a player that, that really excites you as a coach

00:05:16.524 --> 00:05:18.276
cuz you know they're a great teammate.

00:05:18.735 --> 00:05:21.362
- A year or two after I just start talkin',

00:05:21.362 --> 00:05:22.905
I was, like, watching a game. I was just like,

00:05:22.905 --> 00:05:25.366
"Dad, I wanna play basketball."

00:05:25.366 --> 00:05:28.161
- And I was like, " I don't think so."

00:05:28.161 --> 00:05:30.455
The Arkansas Hawks, the little boys, they just

00:05:30.455 --> 00:05:33.499
kept tryin' to, you know, bring him in. And then

00:05:33.499 --> 00:05:35.543
I had to stop myself, because

00:05:35.543 --> 00:05:38.921
I was gonna put limits on him.

00:05:38.921 --> 00:05:41.799
I thought about social skills, because we were

00:05:41.799 --> 00:05:42.884
his only friends.

00:05:42.884 --> 00:05:45.595
♪♪♪

00:05:45.595 --> 00:05:46.804
- I was bullied because I wouldn't

00:05:46.804 --> 00:05:49.807
understand stuff. It took me a minute to figure out,

00:05:49.807 --> 00:05:51.768
like, this person is not my friend.

00:05:51.768 --> 00:05:55.480
I'd be gettin' bullied, but I'd be laughin'. I didn't

00:05:55.480 --> 00:05:57.815
understand, like, "Hey, Kalin you're being bullied."

00:05:58.274 --> 00:06:01.235
They would call him the R word.

00:06:01.235 --> 00:06:02.487
They were really just bein'

00:06:02.487 --> 00:06:04.530
really, really mean to him.

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:08.201
One day, I went into his room, and

00:06:08.201 --> 00:06:12.413
he had, like, a belt around his neck, and he said

00:06:12.413 --> 00:06:16.042
"I'm just—I was just playin',"

00:06:16.042 --> 00:06:17.668
but his throat was sore.

00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:19.879
- I said, "Mama, I, I don't like havin' autism."

00:06:19.879 --> 00:06:22.006
I said more blunt words.

00:06:22.006 --> 00:06:25.718
- I just took the hinges off the door. That was

00:06:25.718 --> 00:06:27.887
him tired of being bullied.

00:06:28.429 --> 00:06:30.431
- And then she grabbed me in my face, she said,

00:06:30.431 --> 00:06:33.810
"Do not hate it. Embrace it. Do you really think

00:06:33.810 --> 00:06:37.688
that you're the person you are now, just because

00:06:37.688 --> 00:06:39.148
of one little thing?"

00:06:39.148 --> 00:06:40.566
I was like, "No, ma'am." She said,

00:06:40.566 --> 00:06:42.652
"Be proud of who you are."

00:06:42.652 --> 00:06:45.196
♪♪♪

00:06:45.196 --> 00:06:47.865
- [Kalin:] I just had my first week of practice.

00:06:47.865 --> 00:06:52.453
[Shoes squeaking]

00:06:52.453 --> 00:06:53.746
-A lotta you guys today, there was

00:06:53.746 --> 00:06:56.374
a noticeable execution improvement

00:06:56.374 --> 00:06:58.793
today. Noticeable from just one day.

00:06:58.793 --> 00:06:59.335
Great job.

00:06:59.335 --> 00:07:00.336
- Team on three. One, two, three...

00:07:00.336 --> 00:07:00.878
- [Together:] Team!

00:07:00.878 --> 00:07:01.462
Awesome.

00:07:02.213 --> 00:07:05.383
- Sometimes I just eat by myself.

00:07:05.383 --> 00:07:08.302
Cuz I don't know a lot of people here.

00:07:08.302 --> 00:07:11.013
I'm still trying to get to know everybody.

00:07:11.013 --> 00:07:14.684
The biggest transition is bein' able to

00:07:14.684 --> 00:07:17.311
just be yourself, just keep doin' things that

00:07:17.311 --> 00:07:19.021
I'm supposed to do. You gotta find your

00:07:19.021 --> 00:07:21.065
own circle. The circle just won't come to you.

00:07:21.732 --> 00:07:24.527
- I'm tryin' to recruit the best, you know,

00:07:24.527 --> 00:07:27.530
basketball players with high character that would

00:07:27.530 --> 00:07:30.491
represent Kent State the best way they can,

00:07:30.491 --> 00:07:31.701
and I saw that in Kalin.

00:07:32.994 --> 00:07:34.745
- Baskeball is his thing,

00:07:34.745 --> 00:07:36.539
but his platform is autism.

00:07:36.539 --> 00:07:39.292
He said, "People already know about it."

00:07:39.292 --> 00:07:41.419
He said, "I want them to accept us."

00:07:43.671 --> 00:07:46.507
The autism program, Miss Gina, I met her.

00:07:46.507 --> 00:07:48.384
I was like, "You have an autism program?"

00:07:48.384 --> 00:07:50.386
She said, "Yeah, it's, like, top ten in the country."

00:07:50.386 --> 00:07:51.345
I said, "You know what?

00:07:51.345 --> 00:07:52.680
I can do something with this."

00:07:52.680 --> 00:07:53.848
- I go, "So, what are your goals?"

00:07:53.848 --> 00:07:56.058
He goes, "Well, I want to come to college,

00:07:56.058 --> 00:07:57.685
get an education."

00:07:57.685 --> 00:07:59.645
He goes, "Number two, I wanna play b-ball.

00:07:59.645 --> 00:08:01.689
And number three, cuz I wanna spread

00:08:01.689 --> 00:08:04.066
autism awareness and help others like me."

00:08:04.066 --> 00:08:06.027
I went—just blew me away.

00:08:06.027 --> 00:08:07.862
- I was like, "Okay, I guess I'm gonna like it here."

00:08:07.862 --> 00:08:09.864
I know, like, there's gonna be days, like,

00:08:09.864 --> 00:08:12.783
I'm gonna be tired. I'm gonna hate the world.

00:08:12.783 --> 00:08:14.785
But I want those days.

00:08:14.952 --> 00:08:18.080
- I had heard a whole lot of "can'ts" in my life.

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:22.668
"Can't" puts a period on it, and after that, nobody tries.

00:08:23.961 --> 00:08:25.671
- Those are days that's gonna push you,

00:08:25.671 --> 00:08:27.340
and those are days that you think back on

00:08:27.340 --> 00:08:29.008
and be like, "Hey, I was in pain, but it was

00:08:29.008 --> 00:08:30.426
a day that I also got better."

00:08:32.011 --> 00:08:35.264
And I have dreams, I have goals, and I'mma

00:08:35.264 --> 00:08:38.226
do whatever I can to work towards those goals.

00:08:39.101 --> 00:08:43.064
♪♪♪

00:08:43.272 --> 00:08:45.608
- I love, I love the people that I'm around,

00:08:45.608 --> 00:08:47.151
but there's just times where I gotta be in

00:08:47.151 --> 00:08:51.405
my own little world or else my mind goes crazy.

00:08:51.405 --> 00:08:54.116
Cuz I haven't, like, given my brain a break.

00:08:54.116 --> 00:08:57.662
Or, like, I'm so into what I'm doin' that

00:08:57.662 --> 00:09:00.790
I forget, like, as much as I want to hoop,

00:09:00.790 --> 00:09:03.209
I gotta take care of myself first and foremost,

00:09:03.209 --> 00:09:04.252
before anybody else.

00:09:05.002 --> 00:09:08.172
A lotta of times, after games,

00:09:08.172 --> 00:09:10.383
or, like, if I'm in a large crowd of people,

00:09:10.383 --> 00:09:12.134
I'll be like, "You go on ahead."

00:09:12.134 --> 00:09:14.971
I'm still tensed up, still gettin' myself back together

00:09:14.971 --> 00:09:17.098
before I even walk out that door.

00:09:17.098 --> 00:09:18.349
See, that's sensory overload.

00:09:20.017 --> 00:09:23.020
I say, "The bullets are flying and there's a lot going on."

00:09:23.020 --> 00:09:25.898
And I, I didn't use the word "sensory overload".

00:09:25.898 --> 00:09:26.899
And he's lookin' around saying,

00:09:26.899 --> 00:09:28.859
"What's goin' on here?" I'm gonna tell you that

00:09:28.859 --> 00:09:32.238
that happens to a lot of players, okay? Not just Kalin,

00:09:32.238 --> 00:09:34.365
but obviously with Kalin,

00:09:34.365 --> 00:09:36.075
there's a reason it's happening.

00:09:36.075 --> 00:09:38.286
He processes some things differently.

00:09:38.286 --> 00:09:41.789
We have to physically show him what to do.

00:09:41.789 --> 00:09:44.166
- I need to watch this person, and see

00:09:44.166 --> 00:09:46.335
if they do it right or wrong. And if they do it wrong,

00:09:46.335 --> 00:09:47.878
I know what not to do. If they do it right,

00:09:47.878 --> 00:09:49.171
I do the same exact thing.

00:09:51.716 --> 00:09:55.720
- There's a lot more similarities to

00:09:55.720 --> 00:09:57.680
the other guys on the roster

00:09:57.680 --> 00:09:59.682
than there are differences.

00:09:59.682 --> 00:10:01.225
- In the MAC, you gotta, you gotta have

00:10:01.225 --> 00:10:02.059
a bunch of guys that can play

00:10:02.059 --> 00:10:02.893
at the high, major level

00:10:02.893 --> 00:10:05.229
or you're not winning like we have here.

00:10:05.229 --> 00:10:07.815
So, he's gonna have to adjust to the physicality,

00:10:07.815 --> 00:10:11.110
the speed, the intensity. And that's just—that’s

00:10:11.110 --> 00:10:13.738
all part of anybody comin' into this program.

00:10:13.738 --> 00:10:16.532
- Everything has been turned up ten times higher.

00:10:16.532 --> 00:10:19.660
The speed? Ten times higher. Attention to detail,

00:10:19.660 --> 00:10:22.371
that's probably, like, the biggest transition.

00:10:22.371 --> 00:10:23.539
I'm still havin' a hard time with that,

00:10:23.539 --> 00:10:26.292
just takin' something and bein' able to just

00:10:26.292 --> 00:10:28.252
get that maintained in my mind.

00:10:28.252 --> 00:10:30.087
It's just movin' on and makin' sure

00:10:30.087 --> 00:10:31.380
I do it again.

00:10:31.380 --> 00:10:34.342
- There you go, that's how every rep should look

00:10:34.342 --> 00:10:36.302
♪♪♪

00:10:37.053 --> 00:10:40.556
Kalin, every rep like that! Every rep.

00:10:40.973 --> 00:10:43.142
As a coach, there are certain things that

00:10:43.142 --> 00:10:45.144
you feel like you can teach, and there are

00:10:45.144 --> 00:10:47.313
certain things that, you know, either you have

00:10:47.313 --> 00:10:48.689
or you don't have.

00:10:48.856 --> 00:10:50.483
- He's very hard to guard one-on-one.

00:10:50.483 --> 00:10:52.360
He can score over either shoulder.

00:10:52.360 --> 00:10:54.487
He's got a soft touch, but he's also got power.

00:10:54.487 --> 00:10:55.696
Somethin' that's different with Kalin,

00:10:55.696 --> 00:10:58.157
you look at him, you think he'll be a rim-level guy.

00:10:58.157 --> 00:11:01.577
He actually has really good burst and athletic ability.

00:11:05.873 --> 00:11:08.334
- He's working every day. He's seeing

00:11:08.334 --> 00:11:10.920
small improvements every day. And if he can

00:11:10.920 --> 00:11:13.506
continue to do that, you know, day after day

00:11:13.506 --> 00:11:14.799
we'll see great things out of him.

00:11:17.259 --> 00:11:19.345
- I wanna be on the AP Top 10.

00:11:19.345 --> 00:11:21.263
I wanna win MAC Player of the Year.

00:11:21.263 --> 00:11:23.015
I wanna be like Zion, win every single

00:11:23.015 --> 00:11:25.351
award known to man somehow.

00:11:25.351 --> 00:11:27.061
I can achieve those goals.

00:11:27.061 --> 00:11:28.062
There's no doubt in my mind

00:11:28.062 --> 00:11:29.939
that I can achieve them.

00:11:29.939 --> 00:11:31.315
It's just a matter of me havin' to work.

00:11:34.443 --> 00:11:35.945
[Crowd cheering]

00:11:35.945 --> 00:11:37.738
- [Announcer:] Kalin Bennett!

00:11:37.738 --> 00:11:40.741
- The first two of Kalin Bennett's career.

00:11:42.243 --> 00:11:44.036
[Bell ringing]

00:11:44.036 --> 00:11:46.038
- I just look at him, and I just smile,

00:11:46.038 --> 00:11:47.915
and he's like,  "Whatchu lookin’ at, Mama?"

00:11:47.915 --> 00:11:52.211
You know? I'm so proud of all 6' 11'' of that kid.

00:11:52.211 --> 00:11:55.089
Sure, I have autism, but I embraced it.

00:11:55.089 --> 00:11:56.340
I embrace who I am.

00:11:56.340 --> 00:11:57.800
